1
00:00:19,811 --> 00:00:20,854
Next, please.

2
00:00:20,937 --> 00:00:21,771
‎JUNKO TAMAI - MINISTRY OF FINANCE

3
00:00:33,199 --> 00:00:35,577
Mo… Mori!

4
00:00:46,379 --> 00:00:47,714
MORI MACHI - CUSTOMS

5
00:00:49,966 --> 00:00:50,800
What?

6
00:00:59,100 --> 00:01:01,770
IMMIGRATION OFFICER (MINISTRY OF JUSTICE)
KEIICHIRO HAYAMI

7
00:01:03,271 --> 00:01:04,439
‎What?

8
00:01:21,748 --> 00:01:22,999
<i>I keep telling you.</i>

9
00:01:23,083 --> 00:01:26,252
Stick to inspection procedures.
Don't do unnecessary things.

10
00:01:26,336 --> 00:01:27,253
‎Yes…

11
00:01:27,337 --> 00:01:30,840
Mori, whenever something catches your eye,
you hyper-focus on it, don't you?

12
00:01:30,924 --> 00:01:33,051
And everything else
goes completely out of focus.

13
00:01:33,134 --> 00:01:34,719
Have you always been like that?

14
00:01:34,803 --> 00:01:37,764
Yes. I used to get scolded
at my previous job too.

15
00:01:37,847 --> 00:01:39,098
-Your previous job?
-Yes.

16
00:01:39,182 --> 00:01:42,644
-Come to think of it, where did you--
-Everyone, look!

17
00:01:42,727 --> 00:01:46,272
Ta-da! Tickets
to the Hi-Fi Unicorn concert!

18
00:01:46,356 --> 00:01:48,399
Amazing! You got Hi-Fi tickets?

19
00:01:48,483 --> 00:01:50,735
So Tamai missed out on the Hi-Fi tickets?

20
00:01:50,819 --> 00:01:54,405
-Don't mention that.
-Hi-Fi's coming to Japan today.

21
00:01:55,156 --> 00:01:56,741
Um…

22
00:01:57,909 --> 00:02:00,370
What is Hi-Fi?

23
00:02:00,453 --> 00:02:01,871
‎What?

24
00:02:02,664 --> 00:02:04,207
-You don't know Hi-Fi?
-No.

25
00:02:04,290 --> 00:02:05,959
You know, the ones who hold the fans.

26
00:02:06,042 --> 00:02:07,127
‎Look.

27
00:02:08,336 --> 00:02:13,299
Hi-Fi Unicorn.
A TJ Produced Korean idol group.

28
00:02:13,383 --> 00:02:15,343
It's their first Japan tour in a year.

29
00:02:15,426 --> 00:02:17,178
They set off fireworks
at their concerts, right?

30
00:02:17,262 --> 00:02:19,389
Just seeing that would make me so happy.

31
00:02:20,223 --> 00:02:22,100
8:30. I won't be able to make it…

32
00:02:22,183 --> 00:02:25,353
They're world-famous, look.

33
00:02:30,942 --> 00:02:32,318
You all know a lot about them.

34
00:02:32,402 --> 00:02:35,155
More like, how does a walking encyclopedia
like you not know about them?

35
00:02:35,238 --> 00:02:37,323
Ah, I don't know much about recent stuff.

36
00:02:37,949 --> 00:02:41,703
Won't they be passing through your gate?

37
00:02:41,786 --> 00:02:44,414
-Can you get me an autograph?
-Absolutely not.

38
00:02:44,497 --> 00:02:46,040
Work is work.

39
00:02:46,124 --> 00:02:49,085
First of all, VIPs have a dedicated route,
so they won't be coming to us.

40
00:02:49,168 --> 00:02:51,421
Where's the romance?

41
00:02:51,504 --> 00:02:53,089
If you want romance, go watch their show.

42
00:02:53,673 --> 00:02:56,885
-That's a good one!
-Right, right.

43
00:03:04,350 --> 00:03:06,436
Um…

44
00:03:06,519 --> 00:03:09,439
Hayami, thank you for earlier.

45
00:03:10,565 --> 00:03:11,649
It's nothing.

46
00:03:15,486 --> 00:03:16,529
Um, Mori…

47
00:03:18,114 --> 00:03:19,657
What was your previous job?

48
00:03:20,533 --> 00:03:22,368
-Um…
-This is terrible!

49
00:03:23,369 --> 00:03:27,957
This is terrible! There's
a system failure on the VIP route.

50
00:03:28,708 --> 00:03:31,169
-What?
-What about Hi-Fi's entry procedures?

51
00:03:31,252 --> 00:03:33,379
The only booths available right now are…

52
00:03:47,268 --> 00:03:49,771
-Please step back, for your safety.
-Please step back!

53
00:03:51,189 --> 00:03:54,108
-It's not safe.
-Clear the way!

54
00:03:54,192 --> 00:03:57,153
Why are there fans here?

55
00:03:57,237 --> 00:03:59,072
-They're from the same flight.
-Please step back!

56
00:03:59,155 --> 00:04:02,867
We asked them to wait
so we could let you all through first.

57
00:04:13,795 --> 00:04:16,798
‎HI-FI UN!CORN - BOY BAND

58
00:04:16,881 --> 00:04:18,299
It's really them.

59
00:04:19,092 --> 00:04:22,303
This is Hi-Fi Unicorn.

60
00:04:23,012 --> 00:04:25,223
Work. This is work.

61
00:04:26,266 --> 00:04:28,935
What are we waiting for? Hurry it up.

62
00:04:29,018 --> 00:04:30,436
I'm very sorry.

63
00:04:30,520 --> 00:04:31,396
What?

64
00:04:32,063 --> 00:04:33,147
Their concert is soon.

65
00:04:33,231 --> 00:04:35,858
-Please speed up the entry procedures.
-Yes.

66
00:04:35,942 --> 00:04:36,776
Can I go?

67
00:04:38,111 --> 00:04:38,945
‎This way, please.

68
00:04:40,280 --> 00:04:41,823
‎Please wait a moment.

69
00:04:41,906 --> 00:04:44,117
-Passport, please.
-Everyone, please wait a little longer!

70
00:04:44,200 --> 00:04:47,161
This time it's mainly
identity verification.

71
00:04:47,245 --> 00:04:49,747
-It shouldn't take long.
-Yes.

72
00:04:49,831 --> 00:04:51,791
I never expected things
to turn out like this.

73
00:04:51,874 --> 00:04:55,086
Handling the unexpected
is what Gate 24 is all about.

74
00:04:55,169 --> 00:04:56,296
Go ahead.

75
00:05:01,884 --> 00:05:03,970
Everything is in order. Welcome to Japan.

76
00:05:10,101 --> 00:05:12,228
Tamai is in full work mode.

77
00:05:13,104 --> 00:05:15,064
Her fangirl mode
is completely sealed away.

78
00:05:16,190 --> 00:05:17,150
Okay.

79
00:05:26,492 --> 00:05:28,328
What's wrong, Hyeongyul?

80
00:05:28,411 --> 00:05:30,913
I think I left my passport somewhere.

81
00:05:31,539 --> 00:05:32,665
Calm down and look for it.

82
00:05:32,749 --> 00:05:34,167
Okay.

83
00:05:35,376 --> 00:05:36,544
Let me help you.

84
00:05:38,546 --> 00:05:39,797
-Thank you very much.
-It's okay.

85
00:05:43,885 --> 00:05:45,053
Thank you.

86
00:05:50,850 --> 00:05:52,727
Mori, stop that already.

87
00:06:01,778 --> 00:06:03,404
Machi Mori?

88
00:06:06,157 --> 00:06:08,826
I thought it was you! It's me, Yuki.

89
00:06:12,580 --> 00:06:13,539
Miss Yuki.

90
00:06:15,374 --> 00:06:16,417
‎Yes.

91
00:06:17,001 --> 00:06:20,671
Miss Yuki! It's me, Chika!

92
00:06:20,755 --> 00:06:22,465
-Kumagawa?
-Yes!

93
00:06:22,548 --> 00:06:24,675
Do you know each other?

94
00:06:25,510 --> 00:06:27,887
I used to teach at a Japanese school.
They were my students.

95
00:06:27,970 --> 00:06:29,847
What a wonderful coincidence.

96
00:06:29,931 --> 00:06:32,809
We're basically Yuki's students too.

97
00:06:32,892 --> 00:06:33,935
So we're friends!

98
00:06:34,018 --> 00:06:36,604
-Friends, friends.
-Friends…

99
00:06:38,689 --> 00:06:40,817
Wow, I'm so jealous.

100
00:06:41,818 --> 00:06:44,946
-Wait, Mori, you lived overseas?
-Yes.

101
00:06:45,029 --> 00:06:46,948
I didn't expect to meet you here.

102
00:06:47,698 --> 00:06:49,242
It's been a long time, Miss Yuki.

103
00:06:50,159 --> 00:06:52,829
-I'm a manager now.
-Yuki.

104
00:06:54,247 --> 00:06:55,581
Yes.

105
00:06:55,665 --> 00:06:57,333
Hyeongyul, where is your passport?

106
00:06:57,917 --> 00:06:58,960
The thing is…

107
00:07:05,383 --> 00:07:06,592
He doesn't have his passport?

108
00:07:08,052 --> 00:07:08,970
Okay!

109
00:07:09,637 --> 00:07:10,847
You don't have it?

110
00:07:11,848 --> 00:07:13,141
Look for it carefully.

111
00:07:13,224 --> 00:07:15,351
Is someone holding it for him?

112
00:07:15,435 --> 00:07:16,727
For now, send them
to secondary inspection.

113
00:07:16,811 --> 00:07:19,313
Have the ones waiting go ahead.

114
00:07:19,397 --> 00:07:20,231
-Yes, sir.
-Yes, sir.

115
00:07:21,357 --> 00:07:23,192
Please guide the passengers.

116
00:07:23,276 --> 00:07:24,819
Everyone, please step
this way for a moment.

117
00:07:24,902 --> 00:07:25,820
‎Yes, sir.

118
00:07:25,903 --> 00:07:28,739
Wait! He's the real Hyeongyul.

119
00:07:28,823 --> 00:07:30,992
Just let him through!

120
00:07:31,075 --> 00:07:32,743
-President…
-Shut up.

121
00:07:32,827 --> 00:07:36,956
I'm very sorry, but no matter who it is,
we cannot permit entry without a passport.

122
00:07:37,039 --> 00:07:39,208
We perform at six p.m.

123
00:07:39,292 --> 00:07:41,752
Who's going to take
responsibility if we don't make it?

124
00:07:41,836 --> 00:07:42,879
Will you?

125
00:07:44,297 --> 00:07:46,507
-Don't you know Hi-Fi?
-You can come this way too.

126
00:07:46,591 --> 00:07:50,553
We'll give you the document later, okay?

127
00:07:50,636 --> 00:07:53,055
Just let him through. Please.

128
00:07:55,141 --> 00:07:57,643
-So?
-He dropped it in the walkway.

129
00:07:58,561 --> 00:07:59,896
The walkway?

130
00:08:00,563 --> 00:08:02,648
I dropped my bag.

131
00:08:03,608 --> 00:08:05,276
Hyeongyul!

132
00:08:06,944 --> 00:08:08,571
<i>Could I have dropped it then?</i>

133
00:08:12,158 --> 00:08:13,493
No passports in the walkway.

134
00:08:15,369 --> 00:08:17,538
So maybe someone picked it up.

135
00:08:20,082 --> 00:08:23,294
Which means…

136
00:08:27,798 --> 00:08:30,134
It's someone among them?

137
00:08:38,142 --> 00:08:39,560
Oh my.

138
00:08:46,984 --> 00:08:50,154
I hear the VIP processing
has ground to a halt.

139
00:08:51,489 --> 00:08:53,616
And of all places, they're at Gate 24!

140
00:08:53,699 --> 00:08:55,910
-Of all places?
-Ah, no…

141
00:08:55,993 --> 00:09:00,665
This Japanese concert tour is part
of a cultural exchange effort with Korea.

142
00:09:00,748 --> 00:09:02,375
Overseas media have their eyes on it.

143
00:09:03,167 --> 00:09:04,210
The scale is in the hundreds of millions.

144
00:09:04,293 --> 00:09:08,172
If the show gets disrupted, it becomes
a major diplomatic and economic issue.

145
00:09:08,256 --> 00:09:09,715
Are you at least aware of that?

146
00:09:11,175 --> 00:09:13,010
Anyway, just take care of it.

147
00:09:13,094 --> 00:09:14,136
‎TAKAHIRO IKEURA
‎DIRECTOR OF KANTO INTERNATIONAL AIRPORT

148
00:09:18,224 --> 00:09:20,434
-Please handle things on the floor.
-Yes.

149
00:09:23,854 --> 00:09:25,773
To all inspection booths.

150
00:09:25,856 --> 00:09:29,235
There is a possibility that a passenger
picked up the missing passport.

151
00:09:29,318 --> 00:09:32,363
<i>Please politely check</i>
<i>with passengers at each booth.</i>

152
00:09:32,446 --> 00:09:33,447
Roger that.

153
00:09:35,366 --> 00:09:37,201
-Tamai.
-Step here, please.

154
00:09:37,285 --> 00:09:38,995
Let's continue inspecting.

155
00:09:39,078 --> 00:09:39,996
Yes.

156
00:09:40,079 --> 00:09:41,581
IMMIGRATION TICKET EXAMINATION SYSTEM

157
00:10:08,941 --> 00:10:11,527
-A camera, a telephoto lens.
-Yes.

158
00:10:16,198 --> 00:10:17,700
Step here, please.

159
00:10:17,783 --> 00:10:19,660
I'll check your passport.

160
00:10:29,045 --> 00:10:30,171
Mira Tono, right?

161
00:10:31,088 --> 00:10:33,132
You're returning from South Korea, right?

162
00:10:33,799 --> 00:10:35,259
I live over there permanently.

163
00:10:37,637 --> 00:10:38,679
Welcome back.

164
00:10:41,390 --> 00:10:42,433
Is something wrong?

165
00:10:50,900 --> 00:10:52,526
MIRA TONO

166
00:10:52,610 --> 00:10:54,612
PORTRAIT
FINGERPRINTS

167
00:11:13,631 --> 00:11:18,469
You know, food this good is always better
when you share it with someone.

168
00:11:18,552 --> 00:11:20,096
So, wanna try some?

169
00:11:21,347 --> 00:11:23,349
You can't bring that into Japan.

170
00:11:24,392 --> 00:11:25,267
Oh, really?

171
00:11:26,185 --> 00:11:28,104
-He's got a lot more!
-What?

172
00:11:28,187 --> 00:11:32,650
Bacon, salami, sausage…
These are all not allowed.

173
00:11:32,733 --> 00:11:35,027
All of them? Wow.

174
00:11:35,736 --> 00:11:38,280
That's impressive.

175
00:11:43,786 --> 00:11:45,454
MIRA TONO

176
00:11:45,538 --> 00:11:47,998
Excuse me, ma'am, about this…

177
00:11:49,417 --> 00:11:50,418
I had plastic surgery.

178
00:11:53,045 --> 00:11:54,839
Do you have
a post-operative certificate or…

179
00:11:54,922 --> 00:11:57,842
No, the surgery was about a year ago.

180
00:12:00,678 --> 00:12:03,681
-Then at exit control, how did--
-I just told them I used lots of makeup.

181
00:12:05,850 --> 00:12:08,561
Departure control is pretty lenient
in most countries.

182
00:12:09,770 --> 00:12:13,649
If we cannot verify that you
are the passport holder,

183
00:12:13,732 --> 00:12:16,402
-we cannot grant you entry.
-What?

184
00:12:16,485 --> 00:12:18,737
The Hi-Fi concert is tonight.
Let me through!

185
00:12:18,821 --> 00:12:21,532
-Oh, uh, well…
-Hey!

186
00:12:21,615 --> 00:12:23,701
-Hurry it up!
-Um, okay, uh…

187
00:12:23,784 --> 00:12:25,453
Um, please wait a moment.

188
00:12:29,665 --> 00:12:31,667
Why is everyone getting
let through except me?

189
00:12:31,750 --> 00:12:34,086
You are right, but, um…

190
00:12:34,170 --> 00:12:36,255
The surgery… Ah, excuse me.

191
00:12:37,131 --> 00:12:40,009
Well, you see…

192
00:12:40,092 --> 00:12:41,218
you've had surgery, but…

193
00:12:47,850 --> 00:12:50,394
Crazy day.

194
00:12:50,478 --> 00:12:52,062
It's just one thing after another.

195
00:12:54,982 --> 00:12:56,025
What should we do?

196
00:13:00,029 --> 00:13:01,322
Knew you'd say that.

197
00:13:01,405 --> 00:13:04,241
Or so I'd like to say.

198
00:13:05,534 --> 00:13:08,078
But I think we all need
to help deal with this problem.

199
00:13:08,662 --> 00:13:10,873
It's rare for you to say
something like that, Hayami.

200
00:13:13,125 --> 00:13:14,835
I just want to get this over with.

201
00:13:17,963 --> 00:13:19,882
This is the last passenger.

202
00:13:20,758 --> 00:13:22,134
Your passport, please.

203
00:13:25,429 --> 00:13:26,514
THREE-WAY IMMIGRATION
PASSPORT READING SYSTEM

204
00:13:26,597 --> 00:13:28,057
HAORU

205
00:13:28,140 --> 00:13:31,685
Rensi Haoru, correct?
What is the purpose of your visit?

206
00:13:32,978 --> 00:13:34,271
I have no idea.

207
00:13:35,481 --> 00:13:38,734
-Pardon?
-Is this Japan?

208
00:13:39,485 --> 00:13:41,737
-Yes.
-Let me think a little…

209
00:13:41,820 --> 00:13:43,864
This is Kanto International Airport.

210
00:13:43,948 --> 00:13:46,450
Why am I here?

211
00:14:01,966 --> 00:14:04,134
It might be stress-induced amnesia.

212
00:14:04,218 --> 00:14:05,678
Amnesia.

213
00:14:06,303 --> 00:14:09,014
A condition where
a portion of memory is lost.

214
00:14:10,808 --> 00:14:13,602
His vital signs are stable,
so let's observe him for a while.

215
00:14:14,478 --> 00:14:15,729
Okay.

216
00:14:15,813 --> 00:14:18,732
I'm sorry. Would it be all right
if he stays here with you all as well?

217
00:14:18,816 --> 00:14:21,235
-Of course.
-Are you all right, sir?

218
00:14:22,570 --> 00:14:23,696
Are you all right?

219
00:14:29,243 --> 00:14:32,788
Um… Are you feeling okay?

220
00:14:33,789 --> 00:14:35,791
-What?
-Do you have a fever?

221
00:14:37,543 --> 00:14:38,961
Do you feel unwell at all?

222
00:14:39,044 --> 00:14:42,506
Of course he's okay.

223
00:14:42,590 --> 00:14:44,008
He's a professional, isn't he?

224
00:14:44,091 --> 00:14:46,051
-Yes, there's no problem.
-See?

225
00:14:46,969 --> 00:14:49,013
-He seems fine.
-But…

226
00:14:52,349 --> 00:14:55,352
Doctor, could you examine him
as well, just to be safe?

227
00:14:55,436 --> 00:14:56,937
Sure.

228
00:14:59,732 --> 00:15:01,650
Hey, we don't have time for this.

229
00:15:01,734 --> 00:15:03,986
-Just your arm, please.
-You four head to the venue first.

230
00:15:04,069 --> 00:15:07,573
-No, we'll wait here as long as possible.
-What?

231
00:15:07,656 --> 00:15:10,492
We want all five of us
to stand on stage together.

232
00:15:10,576 --> 00:15:12,202
-Yeah.
-Please, President.

233
00:15:16,582 --> 00:15:18,751
Yuki, do you have a moment?

234
00:15:23,422 --> 00:15:25,174
Provisional landing permission?

235
00:15:25,257 --> 00:15:26,675
Yes. However,

236
00:15:27,468 --> 00:15:32,389
it depends on whether the embassy
can issue a passport during their stay.

237
00:15:37,144 --> 00:15:40,648
Please let us know your contact info
and place of stay in Japan.

238
00:15:41,315 --> 00:15:43,776
I'll ask MOFA
how his visa will be handled.

239
00:15:43,859 --> 00:15:44,818
Thank you.

240
00:15:44,902 --> 00:15:46,028
Can you fill this out?

241
00:15:47,029 --> 00:15:47,863
Hello?

242
00:15:51,617 --> 00:15:53,243
Is everything okay there?

243
00:15:54,662 --> 00:15:58,374
Um… That pouch…

244
00:15:58,457 --> 00:16:01,210
This? It's official Hi-Fi merch.

245
00:16:01,293 --> 00:16:03,045
-Interested?
-Yes.

246
00:16:03,128 --> 00:16:05,047
The fans had them too.

247
00:16:05,965 --> 00:16:09,635
-And…
-Mori, you really like objects, huh?

248
00:16:10,761 --> 00:16:11,887
You were like that back then, too.

249
00:16:13,555 --> 00:16:14,890
Back then?

250
00:16:16,058 --> 00:16:20,354
<i>Mother crow, why do you squawk so?</i>

251
00:16:20,437 --> 00:16:24,692
<i>Because high on the mountain</i>

252
00:16:24,775 --> 00:16:25,901
<i>I have seven cute…</i>

253
00:16:25,985 --> 00:16:27,277
Stop.

254
00:16:27,903 --> 00:16:29,363
Mori, what are you doing?

255
00:16:31,824 --> 00:16:33,701
Machi, you're reading again!

256
00:16:34,868 --> 00:16:36,412
Chika, it's okay.

257
00:16:36,495 --> 00:16:38,956
ENCYCLOPEDIA

258
00:16:41,250 --> 00:16:42,418
Do you like encyclopedias?

259
00:16:43,377 --> 00:16:45,212
Your father's a scholar, right?

260
00:16:47,673 --> 00:16:49,425
Would you like to sing with everyone?

261
00:16:50,426 --> 00:16:53,178
All your fellow Japanese friends
are gathered here.

262
00:16:53,262 --> 00:16:55,014
Am I Japanese?

263
00:16:55,848 --> 00:16:57,266
I've been to a lot of countries.

264
00:16:58,100 --> 00:17:00,602
The language and the schools
were always different.

265
00:17:01,145 --> 00:17:04,398
But I've never lived in Japan.

266
00:17:04,481 --> 00:17:06,483
Even so, am I Japanese?

267
00:17:08,277 --> 00:17:11,113
<i>I remember it well.</i>
<i>Because you were such a unique child.</i>

268
00:17:12,281 --> 00:17:14,366
Unique?

269
00:17:14,450 --> 00:17:15,743
Maybe you still are now.

270
00:17:17,369 --> 00:17:18,704
What do you think?

271
00:17:35,095 --> 00:17:37,431
Miss Yuka, why did you
choose your current job?

272
00:17:38,766 --> 00:17:42,061
A friend asked me to help out
at an entertainment agency.

273
00:17:43,687 --> 00:17:45,939
That's when I met these boys.

274
00:17:46,523 --> 00:17:49,401
At first, they couldn't
sing or dance well at all.

275
00:17:49,985 --> 00:17:53,572
But as I took care of them,
before I knew it, I became their manager.

276
00:17:54,907 --> 00:17:57,034
I hear they're incredibly popular now.

277
00:17:58,952 --> 00:18:02,289
But perhaps because
they became too popular,

278
00:18:03,207 --> 00:18:04,333
there's been trouble too.

279
00:18:05,834 --> 00:18:08,087
-Trouble?
-Yuki.

280
00:18:08,796 --> 00:18:12,508
-How long are you going to keep talking?
-I'm sorry.

281
00:18:26,396 --> 00:18:27,898
I think by trouble,

282
00:18:27,981 --> 00:18:30,818
she means that concert
in Korea a year ago.

283
00:18:30,901 --> 00:18:32,111
Did something happen?

284
00:18:32,903 --> 00:18:36,698
A lot of stuff happened behind the scenes.
Fans started fighting with each other.

285
00:18:36,782 --> 00:18:38,617
Someone sent a threatening letter.

286
00:18:39,201 --> 00:18:40,202
A threat letter?

287
00:18:40,285 --> 00:18:45,624
"Cancel the concert,
or I'll set fire to the venue."

288
00:18:45,707 --> 00:18:46,750
Whoa…

289
00:18:47,292 --> 00:18:50,546
-What happened?
-Nothing happened,

290
00:18:50,629 --> 00:18:51,922
but they are still wary.

291
00:18:52,506 --> 00:18:57,427
Especially for this concert,
they're all being very careful.

292
00:18:58,303 --> 00:18:59,513
And yet…

293
00:19:02,724 --> 00:19:04,143
What about the passport?

294
00:19:04,810 --> 00:19:06,103
We don't have it yet.

295
00:19:06,186 --> 00:19:10,023
But something's off. With them, as well.

296
00:19:10,858 --> 00:19:14,862
-Do you have, like, a yearbook?
-I threw all that stuff away.

297
00:19:14,945 --> 00:19:17,197
I want to separate myself
from my old self.

298
00:19:17,281 --> 00:19:21,368
So we have nothing
to verify your identity with.

299
00:19:24,580 --> 00:19:27,958
-Oh, this one too?
-This guy is weird too.

300
00:19:28,041 --> 00:19:30,043
He brought over a ton of banned goods.

301
00:19:30,711 --> 00:19:32,171
And he's so confident.

302
00:19:33,463 --> 00:19:36,383
It's almost time for the concert,
but he doesn't look stressed at all.

303
00:19:37,050 --> 00:19:39,595
Yes. That's weird as well.

304
00:19:43,849 --> 00:19:45,434
-Did you just take a photo?
-Huh?

305
00:19:46,018 --> 00:19:47,269
Oh, it's a camera test.

306
00:19:47,352 --> 00:19:49,688
Photography is prohibited here.
Please delete the data too.

307
00:19:51,398 --> 00:19:54,610
-I told you, stop.
-You cannot take photographs.

308
00:19:54,693 --> 00:19:55,861
I'm sorry, sorry, sorry.

309
00:19:58,155 --> 00:19:59,615
Um…

310
00:20:01,325 --> 00:20:03,911
Is that ring an elephant hair ring?

311
00:20:06,038 --> 00:20:08,081
It’s made by weaving hair
from an elephant’s tail.

312
00:20:08,165 --> 00:20:10,584
If it’s real, we need to check it
under CITES.

313
00:20:11,585 --> 00:20:13,170
How much banned stuff are you carrying?

314
00:20:14,713 --> 00:20:18,634
<i>Well, you caught me again. Impressive.</i>

315
00:20:19,843 --> 00:20:21,011
What's with him?

316
00:20:26,516 --> 00:20:29,686
You really do know a lot of things, Mori.

317
00:20:29,770 --> 00:20:31,521
It was an elephant hair ring, right?

318
00:20:32,481 --> 00:20:35,484
I’d seen one before at my previous job.

319
00:20:35,567 --> 00:20:36,985
What was your previous job?

320
00:20:37,569 --> 00:20:38,570
I worked at a museum.

321
00:20:39,529 --> 00:20:41,406
-A museum?
-Yes.

322
00:20:41,490 --> 00:20:43,951
<i>I was in charge</i>
<i>of managing the collection.</i>

323
00:20:44,034 --> 00:20:47,412
<i>I loved being surrounded</i>
<i>by all those objects.</i>

324
00:20:49,539 --> 00:20:53,252
<i>But I used to get scolded a lot too.</i>

325
00:20:54,127 --> 00:20:56,004
This is one of the most

326
00:20:57,089 --> 00:21:00,842
valuable pieces in our collection.

327
00:21:01,510 --> 00:21:03,595
It's an elephant hair ring.

328
00:21:05,847 --> 00:21:08,183
-Please, take a look.
-Um…

329
00:21:09,977 --> 00:21:12,187
That ring may be a fake.

330
00:21:13,188 --> 00:21:15,440
-What?
-If it’s real elephant hair,

331
00:21:15,524 --> 00:21:18,568
each individual strand
should vary in thickness.

332
00:21:18,652 --> 00:21:21,488
But these strands are far too uniform.

333
00:21:23,365 --> 00:21:25,909
The clasp is new too. It’s probably
something made for tourists--

334
00:21:27,744 --> 00:21:30,414
Don't make baseless claims.

335
00:21:30,998 --> 00:21:35,335
You really do have a habit
of meddling, don’t you?

336
00:21:36,545 --> 00:21:37,587
I'm sorry.

337
00:21:39,548 --> 00:21:42,634
I’ve been told that my whole life.

338
00:21:43,760 --> 00:21:45,846
But how did you go from there to customs?

339
00:21:46,638 --> 00:21:48,390
Well…

340
00:21:58,692 --> 00:22:00,152
Got a minute?

341
00:22:05,282 --> 00:22:07,826
Look at that. His sleeve.

342
00:22:11,204 --> 00:22:12,331
Scorch marks?

343
00:22:13,415 --> 00:22:16,043
When we got consent
to check his belongings, TDS

344
00:22:16,126 --> 00:22:17,252
detected traces of gunpowder.

345
00:22:18,211 --> 00:22:21,965
-Gunpowder?
-And we found this in his belongings.

346
00:22:24,134 --> 00:22:25,802
A Hi-Fi Unicorn pouch?

347
00:22:26,762 --> 00:22:27,679
This is what was inside.

348
00:22:29,014 --> 00:22:31,391
Gloves, earplugs…

349
00:22:32,476 --> 00:22:36,021
And a floor plan of the concert venue.

350
00:22:37,272 --> 00:22:40,317
-Why did he have something like this?
-He said he didn't know.

351
00:22:40,400 --> 00:22:43,487
But could it be connected
to what Tamai was talking about?

352
00:22:43,570 --> 00:22:46,490
Last year, someone threatened
to burn down the venue, right?

353
00:22:48,075 --> 00:22:49,242
Haoru…

354
00:22:50,869 --> 00:22:54,122
I don't want to suspect him either,
but we can't just ignore this.

355
00:23:03,757 --> 00:23:05,509
Yes, those numbers…

356
00:23:05,592 --> 00:23:07,427
2026…

357
00:23:07,511 --> 00:23:09,179
Could it have something
to do with today's concert?

358
00:23:10,764 --> 00:23:13,391
-Excuse me.
-Ah, hello.

359
00:23:15,977 --> 00:23:16,895
Excuse me.

360
00:23:16,978 --> 00:23:19,439
I am Ikeura, the airport director.

361
00:23:19,523 --> 00:23:22,317
-How did it go?
-Has there been any progress?

362
00:23:22,400 --> 00:23:24,778
We are currently checking
with the Ministry of Foreign Affairs.

363
00:23:24,861 --> 00:23:28,073
However, we haven't heard back
from the embassy yet.

364
00:23:28,156 --> 00:23:31,409
Regarding the passport,
as of now, there have been no reports

365
00:23:31,493 --> 00:23:33,495
from lost and found or cleaning.

366
00:23:34,454 --> 00:23:36,581
They didn't find my passport?

367
00:23:37,207 --> 00:23:38,917
Let's look one more time.

368
00:23:40,877 --> 00:23:42,045
Right.

369
00:23:42,838 --> 00:23:45,465
Look carefully.

370
00:23:47,717 --> 00:23:50,262
-Search the other side too.
-Let me help you.

371
00:23:50,887 --> 00:23:52,180
-Wait, Mori!
-Don't touch it!

372
00:23:53,765 --> 00:23:54,641
I'm sorry.

373
00:23:55,767 --> 00:23:57,352
-I'm sorry.
-Hey.

374
00:24:01,648 --> 00:24:02,816
Earlier too?

375
00:24:04,985 --> 00:24:05,986
What's this about?

376
00:24:06,903 --> 00:24:08,446
Well…

377
00:24:09,364 --> 00:24:11,741
Mori saw them struggling,
so she just wanted to help.

378
00:24:11,825 --> 00:24:13,827
But that's not part of your job, is it?

379
00:24:14,619 --> 00:24:15,495
No.

380
00:24:17,539 --> 00:24:19,416
I'm very sorry.

381
00:24:19,499 --> 00:24:22,878
A VIP passport is currently missing,

382
00:24:22,961 --> 00:24:27,883
and now an airport staff is going around
touching passengers' stuff.

383
00:24:27,966 --> 00:24:29,384
How do you think that looks?

384
00:24:31,344 --> 00:24:33,680
As I thought, this gate
has far too many problems.

385
00:24:33,763 --> 00:24:36,641
I feel like I've just discovered
part of the reason why.

386
00:24:38,018 --> 00:24:40,979
At this rate, we'll have
to completely reconsider

387
00:24:41,062 --> 00:24:43,481
how this gate is operated, won't we?

388
00:24:46,151 --> 00:24:48,570
Um, um…

389
00:24:48,653 --> 00:24:52,365
-If you want to discuss that, talk to me.
-Counselor…

390
00:24:52,449 --> 00:24:55,785
Our staff caused trouble.
If disciplinary guidance is needed,

391
00:24:55,869 --> 00:24:58,163
-I will handle it later.
-Later?

392
00:24:58,246 --> 00:25:00,624
-The problem is right now--
-Airport Director.

393
00:25:00,707 --> 00:25:02,459
What is the priority issue right now?

394
00:25:02,542 --> 00:25:05,712
-Excuse me?
-Their show is in two hours.

395
00:25:05,795 --> 00:25:08,798
This is no time to be blaming people.

396
00:25:09,716 --> 00:25:11,259
We should look for the passport

397
00:25:11,343 --> 00:25:14,179
and complete all the checks we can, right?

398
00:25:15,639 --> 00:25:18,892
The staff are doing everything
they can right now.

399
00:25:18,975 --> 00:25:20,393
Don't bother them.

400
00:25:21,561 --> 00:25:24,231
Airport Director, let's talk later.

401
00:25:24,314 --> 00:25:26,066
For now, let's keep things moving.

402
00:25:27,609 --> 00:25:30,528
Of course, that's what I was about to say.

403
00:25:30,612 --> 00:25:34,366
I figured as much.
We will keep you updated.

404
00:25:36,034 --> 00:25:39,704
Anyway, just handle this quickly.

405
00:25:43,875 --> 00:25:45,418
Amazing.

406
00:25:46,253 --> 00:25:48,046
She seems different today.

407
00:25:48,129 --> 00:25:49,714
That's true veteran skill.

408
00:25:49,798 --> 00:25:51,841
I think the counselor
is just really angry.

409
00:25:51,925 --> 00:25:55,095
Come on. There's no time
to stand around. Get back to work.

410
00:25:55,178 --> 00:25:56,012
-Yes, ma'am.
-Yes.

411
00:26:01,101 --> 00:26:03,186
-Um…
-We'll talk later.

412
00:26:03,270 --> 00:26:04,854
For now, do what you need to do.

413
00:26:06,356 --> 00:26:07,357
Yes, ma'am.

414
00:26:09,859 --> 00:26:10,944
Fukasawa.

415
00:26:13,113 --> 00:26:14,239
Let's go.

416
00:26:21,204 --> 00:26:22,330
Endo.

417
00:26:25,375 --> 00:26:26,251
Look.

418
00:26:27,585 --> 00:26:30,255
We're starting to see his true identity.

419
00:26:32,257 --> 00:26:34,843
This isn't the first time
you brought in contraband, right?

420
00:26:36,052 --> 00:26:37,846
We have a record here.

421
00:26:37,929 --> 00:26:39,139
Liam Lane.

422
00:26:40,265 --> 00:26:41,766
What is the meaning of this?

423
00:26:43,101 --> 00:26:46,271
-You do remember me!
-Huh?

424
00:26:46,354 --> 00:26:50,692
Ever since we met, I haven't
been able to stop thinking about you.

425
00:26:51,818 --> 00:26:53,194
I'm so happy to see you again.

426
00:26:56,573 --> 00:26:58,283
Then what about the Hi-Fi concert?

427
00:26:58,366 --> 00:27:00,660
No, I'm not going.

428
00:27:00,744 --> 00:27:03,788
I just thought this pouch
would make me look like a fan.

429
00:27:04,414 --> 00:27:07,876
-Look like a fan?
-I wanted you to catch me again.

430
00:27:07,959 --> 00:27:14,007
It's my way of showing my devotion.

431
00:27:17,135 --> 00:27:18,136
Here.

432
00:27:22,974 --> 00:27:26,019
All right then, I will hold onto this
as an item subject to inspection.

433
00:27:26,102 --> 00:27:26,936
What?

434
00:27:27,812 --> 00:27:31,191
Also, it seems the purpose of your entry
differs from what you declared,

435
00:27:31,274 --> 00:27:33,026
so Immigration will take care of you.

436
00:27:33,777 --> 00:27:37,822
-Wait…
-Think about the rules more, and me less.

437
00:27:47,957 --> 00:27:52,295
So, if this means the year 2026,
what about the rest?

438
00:27:52,379 --> 00:27:55,048
2029? That's too far into the future.

439
00:27:56,091 --> 00:27:58,676
Skip the rehearsal.
Make sure wardrobe is ready.

440
00:27:58,760 --> 00:28:01,179
We'll still barely make 18…

441
00:28:02,138 --> 00:28:03,640
Six p.m…

442
00:28:09,938 --> 00:28:11,022
Um…

443
00:28:12,982 --> 00:28:15,193
Could this be referring to time?

444
00:28:15,276 --> 00:28:18,613
-Time?
-It's not the year 2026.

445
00:28:18,696 --> 00:28:20,657
It's 20:26, or 8:26 p.m.

446
00:28:21,866 --> 00:28:24,702
8:26 p.m…

447
00:28:25,328 --> 00:28:28,957
What do these 3R, 4B, and 5G mean then?

448
00:28:30,458 --> 00:28:32,710
8:30. I won't be able to make it…

449
00:28:34,838 --> 00:28:38,633
What if they're colors?
R for red, B for blue,

450
00:28:38,717 --> 00:28:40,093
G for gold?

451
00:28:41,010 --> 00:28:43,471
So then, in other words, it means…

452
00:28:43,555 --> 00:28:44,597
Fireworks!

453
00:28:44,681 --> 00:28:47,809
Tamai said fireworks
would go off at the venue at 8:30.

454
00:28:50,311 --> 00:28:51,813
Fireworks…

455
00:28:55,567 --> 00:28:57,152
Haoru, you are…

456
00:28:57,235 --> 00:28:58,445
Fireworks…

457
00:28:59,654 --> 00:29:00,739
I remember.

458
00:29:02,323 --> 00:29:04,659
I'm a pyrotechnician.

459
00:29:04,743 --> 00:29:06,661
My son is a pyrotechnician too.

460
00:29:07,287 --> 00:29:11,750
I came here today to see his fireworks.

461
00:29:15,920 --> 00:29:18,381
This is from him.

462
00:29:18,465 --> 00:29:21,593
-So his son is doing our fireworks?
-Fireworks, huh?

463
00:29:21,676 --> 00:29:24,137
-I'm looking forward to that.
-Yes, me too.

464
00:29:24,220 --> 00:29:27,265
-Thank you.
-Ah, thank goodness.

465
00:29:28,099 --> 00:29:30,560
‎But, where were all of you…

466
00:29:30,643 --> 00:29:34,773
Regarding the passport,
it wasn't in Haoru's luggage.

467
00:29:34,856 --> 00:29:37,442
It wasn't in Liam's luggage either.

468
00:29:38,735 --> 00:29:41,821
Which leaves only one person.

469
00:29:44,073 --> 00:29:46,201
This way, please. I'll take your luggage.

470
00:29:48,161 --> 00:29:49,412
-Thank you.
-Thank you.

471
00:29:56,127 --> 00:29:59,631
Ma'am! Ma'am, ma'am. Please calm down.

472
00:29:59,714 --> 00:30:02,050
-Why?
-You have to wait.

473
00:30:02,133 --> 00:30:03,510
Do you have a minute?

474
00:30:04,427 --> 00:30:08,181
I looked into the fight last year again
and found a video.

475
00:30:14,062 --> 00:30:15,939
What?

476
00:30:16,022 --> 00:30:18,399
No!

477
00:30:22,654 --> 00:30:25,782
Stop filming!

478
00:30:25,865 --> 00:30:27,367
That person!

479
00:30:27,450 --> 00:30:28,618
Stop filming!

480
00:30:30,537 --> 00:30:33,081
Mira, this is you, right?

481
00:30:34,791 --> 00:30:38,628
Around this time, a letter arrived
at Hi-Fi Unicorn's agency saying that

482
00:30:39,337 --> 00:30:42,465
if they didn't cancel the concert,
someone would set fire to the venue.

483
00:30:45,760 --> 00:30:47,345
Are you saying I did that?

484
00:30:48,304 --> 00:30:51,224
If you know anything,
could you please tell us?

485
00:30:52,934 --> 00:30:54,018
You wouldn't believe me.

486
00:30:55,019 --> 00:30:57,564
Wait a minute. Mira,

487
00:30:58,147 --> 00:31:00,984
rather than fighting, it looks like
you're trying to grab her phone.

488
00:31:02,819 --> 00:31:04,028
You're right.

489
00:31:04,112 --> 00:31:06,781
Even though there were two of them,
she didn't back down.

490
00:31:09,576 --> 00:31:12,829
There must have been a reason
for you to go that far, right?

491
00:31:14,414 --> 00:31:16,249
They were the ones who sent the letter.

492
00:31:17,500 --> 00:31:20,962
Those two caused trouble before
and were banned.

493
00:31:22,255 --> 00:31:23,840
Troublesome people, huh?

494
00:31:24,674 --> 00:31:26,593
I tracked them down and warned them,

495
00:31:26,676 --> 00:31:28,553
but then they beat me up.

496
00:31:28,636 --> 00:31:30,805
So that's what caused that commotion.

497
00:31:31,806 --> 00:31:35,018
Are you saying some radical fans did it?

498
00:31:35,101 --> 00:31:36,728
Don't call them fans.

499
00:31:36,811 --> 00:31:39,314
Real fans would never
cause trouble for their idols.

500
00:31:39,898 --> 00:31:43,568
I made them promise never
to involve themselves with Hi-Fi again.

501
00:31:44,235 --> 00:31:46,946
-Oh my.
-She's a model fan.

502
00:31:47,030 --> 00:31:49,073
So, the reason you had
plastic surgery was…

503
00:31:49,157 --> 00:31:51,951
My face was beaten black and blue.

504
00:31:52,035 --> 00:31:53,745
I got settlement money,
so it was done in no time at all.

505
00:31:53,828 --> 00:31:55,622
No time at all…

506
00:31:55,705 --> 00:31:58,666
Well, the police gave me
quite a scolding, though.

507
00:31:59,792 --> 00:32:00,793
The police?

508
00:32:02,712 --> 00:32:04,756
Hey, huh?

509
00:32:04,839 --> 00:32:05,673
TAKAYA IUCHI
INTERNATIONAL CRIMES DETECTIVE

510
00:32:05,757 --> 00:32:06,758
Oh, Chika.

511
00:32:07,717 --> 00:32:12,096
Hey, we looked into it for you.
Stop treating us like your handymen.

512
00:32:12,180 --> 00:32:14,599
-That's a huge help.
-Like I said, we're not your handymen.

513
00:32:16,392 --> 00:32:17,727
I mean, am I right?

514
00:32:17,810 --> 00:32:20,897
Mira Tono, we found
your records from that incident.

515
00:32:22,857 --> 00:32:25,318
Perfect! With this,
we can perform a match!

516
00:32:25,985 --> 00:32:28,029
-Does that mean I…
-You should be able to enter.

517
00:32:28,112 --> 00:32:29,072
Really?

518
00:32:29,155 --> 00:32:31,866
Thank goodness.
Now you can go to the concert.

519
00:32:37,038 --> 00:32:38,289
She's holding something back.

520
00:32:39,332 --> 00:32:42,418
-Is something wrong?
-I'm so glad, but

521
00:32:42,502 --> 00:32:44,796
as a fan, I'm worried.

522
00:32:44,879 --> 00:32:47,966
-I don't know if Hi-Fi will be okay.
-I get it.

523
00:32:48,800 --> 00:32:50,134
What do you get?

524
00:32:57,809 --> 00:32:58,893
We can't wait any more.

525
00:32:58,977 --> 00:33:01,020
We'll do this concert with four people.

526
00:33:01,104 --> 00:33:02,689
Let's go.

527
00:33:06,693 --> 00:33:07,652
Excuse me.

528
00:33:11,155 --> 00:33:13,783
-Miss Yuki.
-Did you find the passport?

529
00:33:13,866 --> 00:33:15,410
No, not yet.

530
00:33:16,619 --> 00:33:17,662
I see.

531
00:33:18,705 --> 00:33:22,500
But, you know, right, Miss Yuki?

532
00:33:23,626 --> 00:33:25,586
You know where the passport is, don't you?

533
00:33:27,171 --> 00:33:29,173
Yuki does?

534
00:33:29,257 --> 00:33:30,174
What are you talking about?

535
00:33:30,258 --> 00:33:34,053
Hi-Fi Unicorn has had an especially
tough schedule recently, right?

536
00:33:34,846 --> 00:33:36,931
Touring all over the world,

537
00:33:37,015 --> 00:33:40,143
then doing a concert
in Japan the day they arrive.

538
00:33:40,226 --> 00:33:41,686
The fans are very worried.

539
00:33:43,271 --> 00:33:47,233
In particular, Hyeongyul
wasn't feeling well.

540
00:33:47,316 --> 00:33:51,195
As the person closest to him,
you must have known that, Yuki.

541
00:33:52,947 --> 00:33:54,490
So what?

542
00:33:54,574 --> 00:33:56,868
Why does that mean
I'm the one holding the passport?

543
00:33:58,828 --> 00:34:00,288
I found it strange.

544
00:34:03,041 --> 00:34:04,542
That pouch of yours, Miss Yuki.

545
00:34:08,212 --> 00:34:11,257
Everyone else checked their bags
over and over again,

546
00:34:11,340 --> 00:34:13,509
trying to find the passport.

547
00:34:14,260 --> 00:34:20,892
But you haven't opened
that pouch even once.

548
00:34:21,851 --> 00:34:23,227
-I did open it.
-No, you didn't.

549
00:34:23,311 --> 00:34:24,353
I did.

550
00:34:25,271 --> 00:34:26,606
You just didn't see me do it.

551
00:34:26,689 --> 00:34:28,775
Yes, I didn't.

552
00:34:30,359 --> 00:34:34,197
But the object itself
says you haven't opened it.

553
00:34:41,287 --> 00:34:42,205
This says it.

554
00:34:47,919 --> 00:34:49,170
A thread?

555
00:34:49,253 --> 00:34:51,631
That piece of thread has been stuck there

556
00:34:51,714 --> 00:34:53,800
the whole time since you arrived.

557
00:34:58,012 --> 00:35:00,932
If you unzipped it,
the thread should have fallen off.

558
00:35:01,015 --> 00:35:02,433
But it’s still there.

559
00:35:07,146 --> 00:35:08,231
I'm sorry.

560
00:35:09,065 --> 00:35:11,442
It’s been bothering me the whole time.

561
00:35:12,360 --> 00:35:16,447
But I was afraid you’d get mad
if I touched your things without asking.

562
00:35:17,782 --> 00:35:20,993
-Yuki, you…
-Yuki…

563
00:35:25,081 --> 00:35:28,000
The first kid I was in charge of…

564
00:35:28,584 --> 00:35:31,629
She loved singing,
worked so desperately hard,

565
00:35:32,713 --> 00:35:35,049
and pushed herself
to the absolute limit for her fans.

566
00:35:36,551 --> 00:35:41,305
But she pushed herself too far
and ruined her health.

567
00:35:43,683 --> 00:35:46,853
I never wanted to let anyone
go through that again.

568
00:35:50,398 --> 00:35:53,317
I knew Hyeongyul was at his limit.

569
00:35:58,865 --> 00:36:01,075
-Are you okay?
-Yes, I'm fine.

570
00:36:01,159 --> 00:36:05,830
<i>But when I thought of the fans waiting</i>
<i>for the concert, I couldn't say anything.</i>

571
00:36:07,707 --> 00:36:08,708
<i>And then, on impulse…</i>

572
00:36:08,791 --> 00:36:09,709
Are you ok?

573
00:36:11,586 --> 00:36:14,172
-Hey, hurry up.
-Coming.

574
00:36:16,340 --> 00:36:19,802
<i>I just wanted him to rest,</i>
<i>even for a little bit.</i>

575
00:36:20,887 --> 00:36:22,221
That's why…

576
00:36:33,232 --> 00:36:34,066
Yuki…

577
00:36:34,775 --> 00:36:38,738
This was the only way you could give
Hyeongyul a break, right?

578
00:36:40,698 --> 00:36:44,493
I'm very sorry.
I intend to take full responsibility.

579
00:36:46,120 --> 00:36:47,371
Miss Yuki?

580
00:36:48,331 --> 00:36:49,498
What responsibility?

581
00:36:50,833 --> 00:36:54,086
You were worried about us, right?
We're okay now.

582
00:36:54,170 --> 00:36:56,130
-Right?
-Yes.

583
00:36:56,881 --> 00:37:00,134
I got some medicine from the doctor,
so I feel much better now.

584
00:37:00,218 --> 00:37:03,012
It's been a while since
we've had time to relax like this.

585
00:37:03,095 --> 00:37:05,723
Thanks to that,
my energy is fully recharged!

586
00:37:05,806 --> 00:37:07,850
I want to go see our fans, now!

587
00:37:07,934 --> 00:37:09,894
Right, let's hurry.

588
00:37:09,977 --> 00:37:11,938
What a relief.
Let's only think about the performance.

589
00:37:13,189 --> 00:37:14,273
President.

590
00:37:15,233 --> 00:37:16,609
I just remembered.

591
00:37:16,692 --> 00:37:19,987
I was the one who told you
to hold onto Hyeongyul's passport.

592
00:37:23,532 --> 00:37:26,327
Guys. Hurry up. We're going.

593
00:37:26,410 --> 00:37:27,245
-Yes, sir!
-Yes, sir!

594
00:37:27,328 --> 00:37:29,830
-We're all going together.
-Yes!

595
00:37:32,041 --> 00:37:33,167
Nice!

596
00:37:34,627 --> 00:37:37,338
-Thank you too.
-What?

597
00:37:37,421 --> 00:37:39,840
You were concerned
about my health, weren't you?

598
00:37:40,633 --> 00:37:41,842
How did you figure it out?

599
00:37:43,594 --> 00:37:44,720
Well…

600
00:37:45,596 --> 00:37:47,765
Mori, stop that already.

601
00:37:53,938 --> 00:37:57,024
I saw an empty sheet of fever medicine.

602
00:37:57,858 --> 00:38:00,653
So I realized you must have had a fever.

603
00:38:02,863 --> 00:38:05,700
I did something unnecessary again.

604
00:38:07,243 --> 00:38:09,036
It wasn't unnecessary at all.

605
00:38:10,997 --> 00:38:12,373
Thank you.

606
00:38:12,456 --> 00:38:14,458
He's important to us,
and you looked after him.

607
00:38:15,084 --> 00:38:16,877
You're a wonderful customs officer.

608
00:38:18,796 --> 00:38:21,799
Thank you very much! All right, let's go!

609
00:38:28,431 --> 00:38:29,890
Welcome to Japan.

610
00:38:32,393 --> 00:38:34,854
Everyone, thank you very much.

611
00:38:34,937 --> 00:38:37,440
-Thank you!
-Thank you.

612
00:38:39,692 --> 00:38:41,610
Welcome to Japan.

613
00:38:43,279 --> 00:38:44,530
Let's move.

614
00:38:44,613 --> 00:38:45,656
Yeah, let's go.

615
00:38:50,661 --> 00:38:54,081
-Looks like they'll make it.
-Yes.

616
00:38:55,333 --> 00:38:59,795
However, I do expect
an explanation. A lengthy one.

617
00:38:59,879 --> 00:39:01,088
-What?
-Yes.

618
00:39:02,006 --> 00:39:04,258
Let's go, shall we, Counselor?

619
00:39:04,342 --> 00:39:08,554
Ah, no, please go ahead first.

620
00:39:16,520 --> 00:39:17,855
You've gotta be kidding me.

621
00:39:19,774 --> 00:39:21,275
My shift was over long ago.

622
00:39:22,234 --> 00:39:23,611
You've gotta be kidding me!

623
00:39:33,996 --> 00:39:35,873
They're doing it!

624
00:39:35,956 --> 00:39:37,792
‎That's amazing!

625
00:39:37,875 --> 00:39:40,419
Seems like the Hi-Fi concert
is going well.

626
00:39:40,503 --> 00:39:42,171
I wonder if Haoru's watching.

627
00:39:43,506 --> 00:39:45,841
Tamai, you couldn't get
an autograph or handshake, huh.

628
00:39:45,925 --> 00:39:47,551
Well, it's just as good.

629
00:39:47,635 --> 00:39:51,764
Idols are idols, work is work.
I'm satisfied with this.

630
00:39:52,556 --> 00:39:53,849
That's brilliant.

631
00:39:53,933 --> 00:39:55,476
‎You're too close.

632
00:39:56,310 --> 00:39:58,437
Do you have an idol you support, Mori?

633
00:39:59,313 --> 00:40:00,481
Idols?

634
00:40:01,315 --> 00:40:05,069
Just having someone like that is enough
to give people the courage to go on.

635
00:40:05,152 --> 00:40:06,904
It gives them vitality in their life.

636
00:40:07,822 --> 00:40:11,450
-I guess you wouldn't get it, Mori.
-She doesn't even know Hi-Fi.

637
00:40:13,035 --> 00:40:14,745
I do understand having someone like that.

638
00:40:16,705 --> 00:40:18,999
Who is your idol in Hi-Fi, Tamai?

639
00:40:19,917 --> 00:40:22,336
-All of them.
-All of them!

640
00:40:22,420 --> 00:40:23,754
Come on. Who is it?

641
00:40:24,463 --> 00:40:28,050
-Me?
-Good work, everyone.

642
00:40:28,134 --> 00:40:30,386
-Mr. Fukasawa!
-Counselor, you too!

643
00:40:30,469 --> 00:40:32,763
Good work, everybody.

644
00:40:33,889 --> 00:40:35,850
How did things go
with the airport director?

645
00:40:35,933 --> 00:40:37,518
We really got chewed out.

646
00:40:37,601 --> 00:40:41,522
He said Gate 24 caused
one problem after another.

647
00:40:42,314 --> 00:40:43,357
I figured he'd say that.

648
00:40:44,775 --> 00:40:45,693
I'm sorry.

649
00:40:47,820 --> 00:40:50,531
What are you sorry for?

650
00:40:52,283 --> 00:40:55,870
Problems occur everywhere, all the time.

651
00:40:57,413 --> 00:41:01,333
It just means our gate
discovers those problems first.

652
00:41:03,169 --> 00:41:05,921
Before those problems get
brought into the country,

653
00:41:07,089 --> 00:41:10,634
you all notice them
and stop them right at the border

654
00:41:12,094 --> 00:41:15,181
That's why I am proud of our gate

655
00:41:16,599 --> 00:41:18,225
and how problematic we are.

656
00:41:22,605 --> 00:41:24,315
With that being said,

657
00:41:24,940 --> 00:41:27,318
peace and quiet is best.

658
00:41:27,401 --> 00:41:28,486
That's true.

659
00:41:31,447 --> 00:41:33,449
I think so too!

660
00:41:34,158 --> 00:41:37,536
Man, another exhausting day!

661
00:41:38,287 --> 00:41:39,371
Good work!

662
00:41:40,498 --> 00:41:43,042
-All right!
-Have a seat.

663
00:41:57,515 --> 00:42:00,184
"You really do have a
habit of meddling, don’t you?"

664
00:42:03,521 --> 00:42:04,480
I'm sorry.

665
00:42:06,482 --> 00:42:08,776
I, uh, apologize.

666
00:42:08,859 --> 00:42:14,156
She gets, uh, too particular about stuff.

667
00:42:14,240 --> 00:42:17,451
What's wrong with that?

668
00:42:21,205 --> 00:42:24,875
It's her job to be particular, isn't it?

669
00:42:24,959 --> 00:42:27,836
Which makes it a wonderful thing.

670
00:42:29,296 --> 00:42:33,926
This museum has
many things that hold value.

671
00:42:35,678 --> 00:42:39,139
A person like you holds a lot of value.

672
00:42:41,183 --> 00:42:45,646
I'd love for someone
like you to be on our team.

673
00:42:47,856 --> 00:42:50,067
Thank you very much for today.

674
00:42:52,570 --> 00:42:57,992
I intend to reform Japan's border control.

675
00:42:58,075 --> 00:43:02,496
Someday, I will create the strongest gate
to protect this country.

676
00:43:34,945 --> 00:43:38,782
MIDORI SUGIHARA

677
00:43:44,496 --> 00:43:45,956
-What's wrong?
-Nothing.

678
00:43:52,004 --> 00:43:54,465
-May I have one?
-Yes.

679
00:44:01,221 --> 00:44:02,097
It's delicious.

680
00:44:23,285 --> 00:44:25,079
‎She was murdered.

681
00:44:25,162 --> 00:44:26,830
<i>‎This was on the victim's smartphone.</i>

682
00:44:26,914 --> 00:44:29,208
‎You knew the victim well beforehand,
‎didn't you?

683
00:44:29,291 --> 00:44:32,711
‎It looks like she chose Matsuyama
‎as her customs officer.

684
00:44:32,795 --> 00:44:33,962
‎We want to know the truth.

685
00:44:34,046 --> 00:44:34,922
‎The truth?

686
00:44:35,005 --> 00:44:37,675
‎He submitted his resignation.

687
00:44:37,758 --> 00:44:38,592
Subtitle translation by: Maslin Friedman
